; error: 10:5: 'inc' is a '[bind @r]' lambda, and calling it changes what its copies share, so it is called through a place that changes, a 'flex' or 'bind' name, which 'inc' isn't
; A '[bind @r]' lambda is copied freely, but calling one changes what its copies
; share, so it is called through a place that changes, as 'xs[0] = 1' needs one.
task main()
    region r
    flex xs = [1, ...] at r
    fixed inc = [bind @r](n: int) -> nothing
        xs[0] = xs[0] + n
    fi
    inc(2)
fi
